This file is a packing list and nothing more. Where it and the delivery
note disagree, the delivery note is correct.


WHAT IS IN THIS FOLDER
------------------------------------------------------------------------
One folder per model, nine in all:

@MODELLIST@

Inside each model folder:

  parquet/        Thirteen Parquet files, one per forecast origin, named
                  ..._00 through ..._12.
  MANIFEST.txt    When the model ran, which version of the software
                  produced it, and which configuration it used.

@FILECOUNT@ Parquet files in all, @BUNDLESIZE@. Every file holds @ROWCOUNT@
rows and five columns. Section @FILESECTION@ of the delivery note,
"The Delivered Files", names and defines the columns.


OPENING A FILE
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Python
  import pandas as pd
  df = pd.read_parquet("dark_river/parquet/@SAMPLEFILE@")

R
  library(arrow)
  df <- read_parquet("dark_river/parquet/@SAMPLEFILE@")


CHECKING THAT THE DOWNLOAD IS COMPLETE
------------------------------------------------------------------------
SHA256SUMS.txt lists every file in this delivery with its checksum. Run
one of these from the top of the folder:

  Linux            sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt
  macOS            shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS.txt
  Windows          Get-FileHash on each file, or use the Python below

  Python, anywhere
    import hashlib, pathlib
    for line in pathlib.Path("SHA256SUMS.txt").read_text().splitlines():
        digest, name = line.split("  ", 1)
        f = pathlib.Path(name)
        actual = hashlib.sha256(f.read_bytes()).hexdigest() if f.exists() else None
        if actual != digest:
            print("MISSING" if actual is None else "CHANGED", name)

Anything missing or truncated is named. Nothing printed means the copy is
complete. A transfer of this size can lose a file without reporting it;
this is how you find out that it did.


